# Coverage artifacts (v8 / lcov output)
coverage/

# oh-my-claudecode transient session state (machine-written JSON, not ours)
.omc/

# Vendored third-party plugin snapshots (dogfood fixtures) — formatted by their
# upstreams, not us. See test/dogfood/*/SOURCE.
test/dogfood/

# API Extractor reports (tool-generated, exact format)
etc/

# Ecosystem-benchmark run artifacts (machine-written JSON) + vendored upstream
# SKILL.md snapshots (pinned by SHA, formatted by their upstreams, not us).
bench/ecosystem/results/
bench/ecosystem/skills/
# Archived canonical run JSON is machine-written archival data — exact bytes, not
# formatter-owned (the README.md alongside it IS prettier-checked).
bench/ecosystem/results-archive/*.json
# Generated leaderboard snapshot (machine-written Markdown table, exact bytes).
bench/leaderboard/RESULTS.md

# The root CLAUDE.md is a vigiles-COMPILED artifact: `vigiles compile` owns its
# exact bytes (an integrity hash over the output gates it in CI). Prettier would
# re-escape markdown (e.g. `skills/*` → `skills/\*`) and desync that hash, so the
# two gates would fight forever. The spec (CLAUDE.md.spec.ts) IS prettier-checked.
/CLAUDE.md
# Same for the scoped compiled instruction files (nested CLAUDE.md build
# artifacts): vigiles compile owns their bytes + integrity hash, not prettier.
/src/CLAUDE.md
/src/core/CLAUDE.md
/research/CLAUDE.md

# Captured audit/dogfood output (a rendered HTML report + its JSON + terminal
# .txt captures) — machine-generated artifacts kept as a reference record, exact
# bytes, not formatter-owned (same class as the bench/ result snapshots above).
research/dogfood/
